---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Verify downloads" description="How to verify document downloads from streisandeffect.org using SHA-256 checksums.">
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">File integrity</p>
    <h1>Verify downloads</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Each hosted file should publish a SHA-256 checksum. After downloading a file, compute its checksum locally and compare it to the value shown on the document page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="checksum-command-heading">
    <h2 id="checksum-command-heading">Checksum commands</h2>
    <table class="meta-table">
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Linux</th><td><code>sha256sum file.pdf</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th>macOS</th><td><code>shasum -a 256 file.pdf</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Windows PowerShell</th><td><code>Get-FileHash .\file.pdf -Algorithm SHA256</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>What a match means</h2>
    <p>
      If your computed SHA-256 value exactly matches the checksum on the document page, your downloaded bytes match the archived copy described by that page.
    </p>
    <p>
      A checksum match does not prove that the original publisher authored the file. Provenance should be evaluated using original URLs, archived captures, publication context, signatures, and external references.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>What a mismatch means</h2>
    <p>
      If the values differ, do not rely on the file. Try another mirror, clear partial downloads, and report the mismatch through the legal/correction process.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
